[[File:Celosia plumosa 01.jpg|thumb|{{taxlink|Celosia argentea var. plumosa|variety|ver=200928}} '''Red Fox''']]

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A common [[species]] of [[fox]], ''[[Vulpes vulpes]]'' native to [[North America]], [[Asia]], [[Europe]] and North [[Africa]]; small, with [[red]]dish [[fur]], but larger than the [[arctic fox]].
# {{lb|en|uncountable|usually capitalized}} Certain varieties of species of genus {{taxlink|Celosia|genus|ver=200928}}, such as of {{taxlink|Celosia argentea|species|ver=160928}}.
#* {{quote-journal|en| title=Britannica Book of the Year| page=321| publisher=Encyclopaedia Britannica, Incorporated| year=1975| passage=The other All-America winners were the Peter Pan Orange zinnia, '''Red Fox''' celosia, Magic Charms dianthus, and Diablo cosmos}}
#* {{quote-journal|en| journal=Bulletin| issue=236-268| author=Pennsylvania Flower Growers| year=1971| passage=Celosia '''Red Fox''' won for its breeder&mdash;T. Sakata, C>P>O> Box 11, Yokohama, Japan&mdash;a Bronze Medal}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Better Homes and Gardens Container Plants You Can Grow| page=37| editor=Better Homes & Gardens, Better Homes and Gardens Editors | year=1978| passage=CELOSIA or COCKSCOMB Cockscomb (crested) and plumosa (feathered) are the common names for the two most common celosias . ... Popular varieties include: Jewel Box', Lilliput, Empress, Gladiator, '''Red Fox''', and Crusader }}
#* {{quote-book|en| title=Annuals: How to Select, Grow and Enjoy| author=Derek Fell| year=1983| page=77| passage=There are two kinds of celosia. Both are tender annuals {{...}} For intermediate height and stems long enough to cut for flower arrangements, grow ''''Red Fox'''', 19 inches high}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Complete Book of Everlastings| page=49| author=Mark Silber, Terry Silber| year=1992| passage=Celosia argentea CELOSIA Centaurea cyanus and C. moschata BACHELOR'S BUTTON and SWEET SULTAN COMMON {{...}} The most useful plumed varieties are Apricot Brandy, Forest Fire, '''Red Fox''' and accidental light yellow colors.| pageurl=https://books.google.ca/books?id=RSS5avXqWNEC&q=%22red+fox%22+Celosia&dq=%22red+fox%22+Celosia&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiOssy684zsAhXNmOAKHdCvAUwQ6AEwDXoECA8QAg}}

